'''Piemont''', often incorrectly spelled '''Piedmont''' ({{IPA|bl|''PEE-mont''}}; {{Langx|scn|Piemunti}}) is a region in southern [[Hesperia]]. It is bordered by [[Las Peñas]] to the north, the [[Castejón Metropolis]] to the southwest, [[Tukupi]] to the south and [[Campostella]] to the west. It has an area of {{convert|87654.83|km2|abbr=on}} making it the 25th-largest region of Balisca. The capital of Piemont is [[Orquívoro]], and its largest city is [[Syracuse]].

The area that became Piemont was first inhabited by groups of [[W:Hunter–gatherers|hunter–gatherers]] 13,000 years ago. The predominant indigenous group at the moment of the arrival of Illypnians were the [[Kurupiranga]].

